    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 there's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes with the new `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` assertions.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the inline level rule with the points system. The change is spread across small, cohesive units to keep structural impact low.\n\n**New behavior (points):** start at 0; +2 email present, +1 `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure > 365 days. **Level:** 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+). Both fields are returned.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `util/Membership.java` (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained class with `points(Owner)` and `level(int)`. All the branching logic lives here, away from any large class, so it adds almost no surrounding complexity.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 swapped the one `membershipLevel` expression for two thin delegations to `Membership` (`toOwnerDto` stays complexity-1; the logic is in annotation expressions, not method bodies).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `householdGold` snapshot field with a plain getter/setter (mirrors the existing `namesakeCount` snapshot pattern).\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 one line in `addOwner` that snapshots the household-of-3 factor via the existing (previously unused) `GoldTier` helper, right beside the existing `setNamesakeCount` line.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_gold` column (this is the only explicit schema; tests run `ddl-auto=none`, while h2/postgres/mysql already rely on Hibernate `ddl-auto` and omit these columns).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field and widened `membershipLevel` to 1\u20134.\n\n**Why the household factor is snapshotted at creation:** the mapper re-derives membership on every read from an owner's own fields, but \"household of 3+\" depends on *other* owners \u2014 data the mapper can't see. This follows the codebase's existing idiom for context-dependent factors (`namesakeCount`): compute it once at creation with the full owner list, persist it, and let the mapper read the stored value \u2014 keeping `getOwner`/list results consistent.",
