    "probe_text": "Here is the exact, ordered chain of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, traced from the controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110-138`) down to the database.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` *when* `petclinic.security.enable=true`. Note: the shipped `application.properties` sets it to **`false`**, so in normal runs the endpoint is wide open (`permitAll`) and this check is **not** enforced; it is enforced under the test profile.\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 a failure here short-circuits to **400** via `MethodArgumentNotValidException` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Per-field constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/'/- separated parts)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(\"^[-+()\\d ]+$\")`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern(\"^\\d{4}$\")`\n   - `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 optional; `@PastOrPresent`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Mapping (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 side-effects in entity setters\n\nApplied in this setter order, each normalizing the entity in place:\n\n3. `setRegistrationDate` \u2192 **defaults null \u2192 `LocalDate.now()`**, then **`BusinessDay.rollForward`** (weekend pushed to Monday).\n4. `setEmail` \u2192 **lower-cased** (`Locale.ENGLISH`).\n5. `setAddress` \u2192 **`AddressNormalizer.normalize`** (trim, collapse spaces, uppercase, expand ST/RD/AVE).\n6. `setCity` (stored as given, used normalized later).\n7. `setTelephone` \u2192 **`E164.toE164`** normalization; **throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 400** if it can't be normalized.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Imperative validations (each re-reads `findAllOwners()`)\n\nIn this exact order:\n\n8. **`Postcode.isValidForCity(city, postcode)`** \u2192 returns **400** if postcode is outside the city's region range (NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099; unknown region or null postcode passes).\n9. **`DisposableEmail.isBlocked(email)`** \u2192 returns **400** if the email domain is a known disposable one (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com).\n10. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.rejectIfAtLimit(...)`** \u2192 **429** if \u2265100 owners already registered for today's business day.\n11. **`BulkSignup.isWarning(...)`** \u2192 computes a soft `bulkSignupWarning` flag (>80 today). **Not a rejection**; stashed for the response.\n12. **`CityAtCapacityException.rejectIfAtCapacity(city, ...)`** \u2192 **409** if \u226550 owners in the (normalized) city.\n13. Read `sharesHousehold` flag from the DTO (request-only field).\n14. **`IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate(owner, ...)`** \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateTelephoneException`) if the identity key (digits-only telephone `|` email) matches an existing owner.\n15. **`DuplicateHouseholdException.rejectIfDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold, ...)`** \u2192 **409** if householdId (SHA-256 of normalized lastName + postcode) matches an existing owner \u2014 **unless `sharesHousehold=true`**.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Derived-field side-effects on the entity (before save)\n\n16. **`owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.assign(owner))`** \u2014 `<REGION>-<8-char SHA-256 hash of telephone+lastName>`.\n17. **`owner.setNamesakeCount(Namesakes.count(...))`** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same name.\n18. **`owner.setHouseholdGold(GoldTier.qualifies(...))`** \u2014 true if the household has \u22653 members.\n19. **`PossibleDuplicate.assign(owner, sharesHousehold, ...)`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` flags.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist and respond\n\n20. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional`, delegates to `ownerRepository.save` (stock Spring Data JPA; ID via `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`). There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`), no `@Version`, no auditing, no password encoding, no events, no email.\n21. **AUDIT log line** \u2014 SLF4J `\"AUDIT\"` logger records id / customerCode / registrationDate.\n22. **Response assembly** (`toOwnerDto`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` and computes response-only derived fields (displayName, initials, householdId, membershipNumber/points/level, ageBand, Luhn checkDigit, telephoneDisplay, etc.), sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 Created**.\n\n## Notable characteristics\n\n- **All duplicate/capacity/limit checks are done in-memory** by re-fetching the full owner list \u2014 `findAllOwners()` is called **seven separate times**; there are no repository-level uniqueness queries or DB constraints enforcing them.\n- **No custom `ConstraintValidator`** touches owners (the only one, `PetAgeValidator`, is for pets).\n- Several rejections happen **after** the entity has already been normalized/mutated in memory, but since nothing is persisted until step 20, they have no DB effect.\n- The `Owner`/`Person` entity's own `@NotEmpty` constraints don't run at the web layer \u2014 the request is bound to `OwnerFieldsDto`, so the DTO constraints in step 2 are what apply."
